The Makefiles for these games require the "dm" program to install-- we've written a dungeon master program (hasn't everybody?) and theyexpect to have it around.  They also require the "mkdep" program tocreate dependencies.  You probably want to note in the posting thatthe problems exist, and everybody should hack the Makefile.Your posting should credit Earl Cohen with writing the logic for cribbage,and Ken Arnold with doing the screen interface.--keith